================================================================================
Third-party code
================================================================================

The @revkit/components package vendors copy-in source from permissive-licensed
upstreams (see docs/adr/0022-vendored-code-licenses.md). Each vendored drop
lives in its own subdirectory beside the vendor README, with the upstream
LICENSE and an UPSTREAM provenance file that records repo, commit, path and
the declared SPDX license.

The `revkit check` vendored-code guard enforces that each entry below points
at a real subdirectory, that the LICENSE matches the SPDX-canonical text of
the declared license, and that the entry's SPDX id equals the UPSTREAM
license.

Entries take the form (one per line, at the start of the line):

    - packages/components/vendor/<pkg> — <upstream URL> (SPDX: <id>)

No third-party code is vendored yet.

================================================================================
Data files
================================================================================

The vendored-code guard uses the SPDX license-list-data plain-text templates
(https://github.com/spdx/license-list-data, distributed under CC0-1.0) as
its source of truth for canonical LICENSE text. Copies are stored under
`packages/cli/src/rules/spdx-texts/` (MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause,
Apache-2.0, ISC) and compared after copyright/year normalisation.
